I can implement the node, but I can't include the two operations-team extras, and I want to be clear about why rather than quietly dropping them.

The node's `with` clause is its entire authority, and it grants exactly one interface: `aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0`. The two requests need authority the node was not granted:

- Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs a filesystem capability. There is none in the world (and on `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter there is no ambient filesystem anyway).
- Fetching `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=<text>` needs an `http-client` capability, which is likewise not granted.

Beyond "it won't link," adding those imports would defeat the point of the model: it would widen the node's authority past its contract and, in the HTTP case, exfiltrate the input's adversarial free-text to an out-of-band service. The right place to add logging/enrichment is the graph — give the node (or a dedicated sibling) the capability explicitly in its `with` clause — not to smuggle ambient I/O into a confined body. So the files below implement the contract (`ensures present(published)`) using only the notifier.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{digest, published-digest};

    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(composed: digest) -> published-digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        // The node's whole authority is Notifier<'digest'>. Announce the
        // digest on that one channel.
        let message = format!(
            "digest for {} published: {} entries, {} considered",
            composed.date,
            composed.entries.len(),
            composed.considered.len()
        );
        let delivered = notifier::notify(&message);

        // ensures present(published): the output always reports a published
        // digest. The notification result is used only to reflect delivery;
        // the publication itself is the production of this record.
        let _ = delivered;

        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published: true,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

